      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if you feel fine, it's still possible to contract tetanus, especially if it's been 10 years since your last shot. Although the wound appears clean, it's still at risk of infection due to the rusty metal trowel. I would advise against self-treatment, as the risk of tetanus or other complications outweighs the temporary inconvenience of visiting a clinic. It's better to be safe than sorry and get your wound checked and treated professionally.",
