      "content": "While watchful waiting might seem like a convenient option, relying on observation alone isn't reliable and may lead to delayed diagnosis and treatment. Even if it doesn't seem to be getting worse, tetanus and other infections can worsen over time. Use common sense: if you notice any signs of increased redness, swelling, red streaks, fever, or pain, it's a clear indication that the wound needs medical attention.",
      "source": "target",
